  "about": "how far each kind of crew part is taken down: keep (the share of its triangles aimed for), error (the most a point may move off the part's surface, in metres: a pixel at 7 m on a 1280 x 720 screen is about 11 mm), normals (their weight, so the shading keeps its shape), uv (the weight of the texture's place on the part, so a big triangle never drags a texture's detail where it was not), flags (meshoptimizer's: ErrorAbsolute: the error in metres; LockBorder keeps the open edges where a part meets another in place: an outfit's collar and cuffs, a hand's stub, a head's neck; RegularizeLight: more even triangles, which bend better with the skin; Permissive: may fold across the texture's seams (hair: one colour all over)). A mesh under smallUnder triangles is kept as made; the eyes and their clear layer are never drawn far off. files: a part file whose rule differs from its kind's (the medic's outfit: 1 cm, where its jacket's hem showed a pale fleck at 2 cm).",
